{"id":149079,"accession_number":"1977.203","share_license_status":"CC0","tombstone":"Kakinomoto no Hitomaro (柿本人麻呂像), early 1300s. Japan, Kamakura period (1185–1333). Hanging scroll; ink and color on silk; painting: 107.6 x 39 cm (42 3/8 x 15 3/8 in.); mounted: 174.4 x 55 cm (68 11/16 x 21 5/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Herbert F. Leisy in memory of his wife, Helen Stamp Leisy, 1977.203","current_location":null,"title":"Kakinomoto no Hitomaro","title_in_original_language":"柿本人麻呂像","creation_date":"early 1300s","creation_date_earliest":1300,"creation_date_latest":1333,"artists_tags":[],"culture":["Japan, Kamakura period (1185–1333)"],"technique":"hanging scroll; ink and color on silk","support_materials":[],"department":"Japanese Art","collection":"ASIAN - Hanging scroll","type":"Painting","measurements":"Painting: 107.6 x 39 cm (42 3/8 x 15 3/8 in.); Mounted: 174.4 x 55 cm (68 11/16 x 21 5/8 in.)","dimensions":{"painting":{"height":1.076,"height_inch":42,"height_inch_fraction":0.375,"width":0.39,"width_inch":15,"width_inch_fraction":0.375},"mounted with knobs":{"height":1.744,"height_inch":68,"height_inch_fraction":0.6875,"width":0.604,"width_inch":23,"width_inch_fraction":0.75},"mounted":{"height":1.744,"height_inch":68,"height_inch_fraction":0.6875,"width":0.55,"width_inch":21,"width_inch_fraction":0.625},"knob diam":{"depth":0.025,"depth_inch":1,"depth_inch_fraction":0}},"state_of_the_work":null,"edition_of_the_work":null,"copyright":null,"inscriptions":[{"inscription":"浦のあさ霧にしま隠れゆく舟をしぞ思","inscription_translation":"Dimly, dimly/ \nin the morning mist that lies over Akashi Bay,/ \nmy longings follow with the ship / \nthat vanishes behind the distant isle.\n\n—Translated by Robert H. Bower and Earl Miner","inscription_remark":null,"sortorder":1}],"exhibitions":{"current":[{"id":309658,"title":"Portraiture: The Image of the Individual","description":"<i>Portraiture: The Image of the Individual</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (November 22, 1983-January 22, 1984).","opening_date":"1983-11-22T05:00:00"},{"id":211775,"title":"Highlights of Asian Paintings from The Cleveland Museum of Art","description":"<i>Highlights of Asian Paintings from The Cleveland Museum of Art</i>. Nara National Museum (organizer) (February 21-March 29, 1998); Suntory Museum of Art (April 28-June 21, 1998).","opening_date":"1998-02-21T00:00:00"},{"id":687098,"title":"Practice and Play in Japanese Art","description":"<i>Practice and Play in Japanese Art</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (June 20-November 30, 2025).","opening_date":"2025-06-20T04:00:00"}],"legacy":[]},"provenance":[{"description":"Mr. Herbert F. [1900–1977] and Mrs. Helen Stamp Leisy [1906–1975], Cleveland, OH, given to the Cleveland Museum of Art","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":"?–1977","sortorder":1},{"description":"The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":"1977–","sortorder":2}],"find_spot":null,"related_works":[],"former_accession_numbers":[],"did_you_know":"The landscapes at the top and bottom of the painting depict Akashi Bay, with its famous pines along the shore, and a lone figure in a boat.","early_education_description":null,"artlens_description":null,"description":"Among Japan’s greatest poets, Kakinomoto no Hitomaro’s (c. 660–724) portrait was often displayed at poetry competitions. Here, he gazes up at a falling cherry blossom, his writing box before him, brush and paper in his hands. A short biography and one of his poems are inked on painted rectangles meant to look like decorated papers. The first part of the poem has been mostly lost, but from what remains, it is possible to recognize it as <br><br>Dimly, dimly<br>in the morning mist that lies over Akashi Bay,<br>my longings follow with the ship <br>that vanishes behind the distant isle. <br><br>—Translated by Robert H. Bower and Earl Roy Miner","external_resources":{"wikidata":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60473344"],"internet_archive":["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1977.203-the-poet-kakinomoto"]},"citations":[{"citation":"<em>Tōyō kaiga no seika: tokubetsuten: Kurīvurando Bijutsukan no korekushon kara </em>[東洋絵画の精華: 特别展: クリーヴラント美術館のコレクションから= Highlights of Asian painting from the Cleveland Museum of Art]. Nara, Japan: Nara National Museum, 1998.","page_number":"Reproduced: p. 92, no. 59","url":""},{"citation":"Levine, Gregory P. A., Andrew Mark Watsky, Gennifer S. Weisenfeld, and Yoshiaki Shimizu. <em>Crossing the Sea: Essays on East Asian Art in Honor of Professor Yoshiaki Shimizu</em>. Princeton, NJ: P.Y. and Kinmay W. Tang Center for East Asian Art, Dept. of Art and Archaeology, Princeton University in association with Princeton University Press, 2012.","page_number":"Reproduced: fig. 4, pp. 142–143","url":""}],"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1977.203","images":{"annotation":null,"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1977.203/1977.203_web.jpg","width":"350","height":"900","filesize":"105491","filename":"1977.203_web.jpg"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1977.203/1977.203_print.jpg","width":"1322","height":"3400","filesize":"1095019","filename":"1977.203_print.jpg"},"full":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1977.203/1977.203_full.tif","width":"3028","height":"7789","filesize":"70784168","filename":"1977.203_full.tif"}},"alternate_images":[{"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1977.203/1977.203_alt0_web.jpg","width":"900","height":"874","filesize":"151471"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1977.203/1977.203_alt0_print.jpg","width":"3374","height":"3275","filesize":"1207862"},"full":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1977.203/1977.203_alt0_full.tif","width":"3374","height":"3275","filesize":"33189872"},"date_created":"2015-02-19T20:25:07.011000","annotation":""},{"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1977.203/1977.203_alt1_web.jpg",